{"question": "Webhook delivery marked failed on transient error
When I trigger a webhook for an order update, the delivery shows status FAILED even though the endpoint was temporarily slow to respond. The mutation returns successfully but the webhook was never actually delivered. I expected the system to retry the delivery rather than permanently marking it as failed.

gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.webhook.mutations.webhook_trigger.WebhookTrigger.perform_mutation"}

{"question": "Bulk delete sales silently accepts wrong object types
When I accidentally pass a product ID instead of a sale ID to the bulk delete sales mutation, I don't get a helpful error telling me I used the wrong type. Instead the mutation appears to succeed but deletes nothing, with no indication that one of my IDs was invalid. I expected a clear validation error listing the offending ID.

gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.discount.mutations.bulk_mutations.SaleBulkDelete.get_promotion_instances"}

{"question": "Webhook and plugin events not triggered after bulk-deleting vouchers
When I bulk-delete vouchers, the deletion succeeds and the vouchers are removed from the database, but the voucher_deleted webhook events and plugin callbacks are never fired. Downstream systems that listen for voucher deletions don't receive any notification. The same bulk-delete operation works correctly for other entity types.

Expected: After bulk-deleting vouchers, all registered webhook events and plugin hooks for voucher_deleted should be invoked for each deleted voucher.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.discount.mutations.bulk_mutations.VoucherBulkDelete.bulk_action"}

{"question": "Signed URLs for file downloads never expire
When I configure an Azure URL expiration time in settings, the generated signed URLs still remain valid indefinitely. Files served through the default Azure storage backend can be accessed by anyone with the URL long after they should have become invalid. I expected the expiration setting to take effect so that temporary access links would time out.

gold_fqn": "saleor.core.storages.AzureStorage"}

{"question": "Confusing error message when providing invalid shipping method ID
When I submit a webhook request with an excluded shipping method that has a malformed ID, the error message shows "Malformed ShippingMethod id was provided: %s" with the literal %s character instead of the actual ID I provided. I have no way to know which ID was rejected.

Expected: the error message should include the actual invalid ID value so I can identify and fix the problematic entry.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.webhook.response_schemas.shipping.ExcludedShippingMethodSchema.clean_id"}

{"question": "Schema export crashes with attribute error on certain types
When exporting or printing the GraphQL schema definition, the process crashes with an attribute error when encountering object types that do not carry a graphene_type attribute. This prevents developers from generating a complete schema SDL dump.

Expected: The schema should print successfully for all types, silently skipping graphene-specific metadata when unavailable.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.schema_printer.print_object_directives_for_category"}

{"question": "Search crashes when filtering products by date-only attribute
When I try to filter products using a custom date attribute that stores only dates (not date+time), the product listing page throws an error and won't load. The same attribute works fine when configured to include time. I expected date-only attributes to work just like date-time ones.

gold_fqn": "saleor.attribute.search.get_search_vectors_for_attribute_values"}

{"question": "Search fails when filtering products by date-only attributes
When I try to search or filter products using an attribute of type "Date" (without time), the search returns no results and sometimes errors out. This works fine for date-time attributes but breaks for plain date attributes. I expected date-only attributes to work the same way as date-time ones.

gold_fqn": "saleor.attribute.search.get_search_vectors_for_attribute_values"}

{"question": "Promotion rule translations appear wrong on some cart items
I have two different products in my cart that both use the same promotion rule. When I view the cart, one product shows the correct rule name and description, but the other shows a different rule's translation — as if the translations got mixed up between the two items. Reloading the page doesn't fix it.

Expected: each cart line should always display the correct promotion rule translation for its own variant listing.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.checkout.dataloaders.promotion_rule_infos.VariantPromotionRuleInfoByCheckoutLineIdLoader.batch_load.with_promotion_translations"}

{"question": "Products don't get re-indexed after deleting a page type
When I delete a page type, products that had attributes referencing pages in that type keep stale search results. Their search index is never updated, so they no longer appear in relevant searches even though their attributes changed.

Expected behavior: those products should have their search index marked as dirty so they are re-indexed with correct data.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.page.mutations.page_type_delete.update_products_search_index"}

{"question": "Custom schedule import runs on every scheduler tick
When Celery beat processes periodic tasks that use a custom schedule, the Python module for each custom schedule is imported and validated on every single tick instead of being cached. This causes noticeable slowdown in the scheduler loop and repeated module loading overhead. I expected the import path to be resolved once and reused across all ticks.

Expected instead: the custom schedule object should be loaded once per import path and then reused from cache for subsequent scheduler ticks.", "gold_fqn": "saleor.schedulers.models.CustomSchedule.schedule"}

{"question": "Dry run crashes with unhelpful error on empty event list
When I submit a GraphQL query that parses correctly but contains no webhook events, the dry run operation crashes instead of giving me a clear message about what's wrong. I expected it to tell me my query defines no events.

"gold_fqn": "saleor.graphql.webhook.mutations.webhook_dry_run.WebhookDryRun.validate_query"}

